                            <comment id="16251105" author="slava.koptilin" created="Tue, 14 Nov 2017 08:54:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;TeamCity looks good enough &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F2981%2Fmerge&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F2981%2Fmerge&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
I could not find test failures that are related to the changes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16254974" author="agoncharuk" created="Thu, 16 Nov 2017 09:03:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I do not think that a silent semaphore release is a good option for client disconnect. If a client disconnects, the semaphores should  throw something like SemaphoreBrokenException and force a user to re-create the semaphore. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16256933" author="agoncharuk" created="Fri, 17 Nov 2017 12:53:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks, merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
